  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "If $g(x)={\\int }_{0}^{x}{t}^{2}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t$ for $x>0,$ determine ${g}^{\u2032}(2).$",
  "worked_solution": "The function ${t}^{2}{e}^{t}$ is continuous on $[0,x],$ where $x>0.$ So, FTC II applies, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{t}^{2}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of ${g}^{\u2032}(2),$ we substitute $x=2$ in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2032}(2) & ={2}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{2} \\\\  & =4{e}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
